-- title:
--   Satz 1 (Hauptsatz) — a point on all extreme supports is a nonnegative combination of $S$
-- statement:
--   Let $S \subset \mathbb{R}^n$ be a finite non-degenerate point system, and let $x \in \mathbb{R}^n$ satisfy every extreme support inequality of $S$:
--
--   $$\langle \alpha, x\rangle \ge 0 \quad \text{for every extreme support } \alpha \text{ of } S .$$
--
--   Then $x$ is a nonnegative linear combination of the points of $S$: $x = \lambda a + \mu b + \cdots$ with $\lambda, \mu, \ldots \ge 0$, where $a, b, \ldots$ are the points of $S$.
--
--   Together with the trivial converse (every nonnegative combination satisfies every support inequality), this identifies the cone generated by $S$ with Weyl's *konvexe Pyramide*, the intersection of the finitely many extreme support half-spaces. It is the finite-generation-implies-finite-intersection half of the Minkowski–Weyl theorem for cones, with the half-spaces identified as the facets.
--
--   **Formalization Note** Weyl's wording "alle extremen Stützungsgleichungen erfüllt" refers to the support *inequalities* $\langle\alpha,x\rangle\ge 0$ (as the proof on p. 292 and Satz 2 make explicit), and that is what the hypothesis states. The hypothesis quantifies over every extreme normal $\alpha$, so positive multiples are included automatically.
-- source:
--   Weyl, Elementare Theorie der konvexen Polyeder, Comment. Math. Helv. (1935), p. 291, Satz 1 (Hauptsatz), (3)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_WeylPolyhedra_Shared_Representable
import Definitions.Def_WeylPolyhedra_Shared_NonDegenerate
import Definitions.Def_WeylPolyhedra_Shared_IsExtremeSupport

namespace WeylPolyhedra.Pyramid

/-- Weyl (1935), §1, p. 291, Satz 1 (Hauptsatz): let `S ⊆ ℝⁿ` be a finite non-degenerate point
system. Every point `x` that satisfies all extreme support inequalities of `S`
(`α ⬝ᵥ x ≥ 0` for every extreme support `α` of `S`) is a nonnegative linear combination of the
points of `S`. -/
theorem hauptsatz {n : ℕ} (S : Finset (Fin n → ℝ)) (hS : Shared.NonDegenerate S) (x : Fin n → ℝ)
    (hx : ∀ α : Fin n → ℝ, Shared.IsExtremeSupport S α → 0 ≤ α ⬝ᵥ x) :
    Shared.Representable S x := by sorry

end WeylPolyhedra.Pyramid
